%description:

A real cell's background UE's CQI, against the closed form.

A background UE is the bgTrafficGenerator's UE of a real base station's NIC.
Its CQIs are what-ifs on the radio medium: in DL a transmission of the base
station's radio at the UE's phantom radio, in UL one of the phantom radio at
the base station's. bgMeasuredSinrDl and bgMeasuredSinrUl are what those
what-ifs report, in dB, as the mean over the carrier's bands.

The scenario is two real cells, with two background UEs in the first and a
real UE, loaded in both directions, in the second. Fading and shadowing are
off, and every link is NLOS by configuration, so everything is a sum of the
radios' constants and one path loss of TR 38.901:

    S_DL = eNodeBTxPower + Gcell + Gbg - cableLoss_bg - PL(d)
    N_DL = thermalNoise + noiseFigure_bg
    S_UL = bgTxPower + Gbg + Gcell - cableLoss_cell - PL(d)
    N_UL = thermalNoise + noiseFigure_cell

The terms are set apart in bgUE[0] (each different from the NED default and
from the corresponding term of the other end), so that a term taken from the
wrong radio or the wrong direction moves the result. bgUE[1] stays on the
NED defaults of its radio and its generator, and pins those.

downlinkInterference and uplinkInterference are the medium's switches of a
real cell's interference at any receiver, and default to false:

 - with both off, nothing else reaches the what-ifs. Both SINRs are one value
   at any load, min = max = S - N, and a real cell's interference does not
   exist for a background UE;
 - with both on, the maximum is still S - N, from the slots in which the other
   cell was idle, and the minimum is S - (N + I), with I from the other cell
   alone: the other gNB's power and gain in DL, the real UE's in UL, at their
   own distances.

Only the path loss is a specification's: that a background UE's links are
evaluated this way, with these budgets, is the model's choice, so this is a
regression test of that choice.

The cell's own allocations are not in I, though the cell's background UEs are
loaded in both directions: a CQI's interference is the transmissions of the
other cells only, and what makes them other cells is the what-if's cellId.
With the DL what-if's cellId replaced by NODEID_NONE, the cell interferes with
its own background UE and the minimum falls by far more than the closed form
says (mutation-checked).

The loads' periods are coprime with the CQI period of 6 slots, so that the CQI
samples every phase of a load's busy and idle slots.

%extraargs: -c BackgroundUeCqi

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config BackgroundUeCqi]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.MultiCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s
seed-set = 0

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false
# The extremes are the quantities under test here, not the average.
**.bgMeasuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.bgMeasuredSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

############### The sweep: the medium's switches of a real cell's interference ##############
**.downlinkInterference = ${dli = false, true}
**.uplinkInterference = ${uli = false, true ! dli}
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

############### Geometry: bgUE[0] and bgUE[1] in the first cell, the loaded real UE in the second ##############
*.gnb1.mobility.initialX = 250m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialX = 750m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].numBgUes = 2
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].mobility.initialX = 350m
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].mobility.initialY = 400m
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[1].mobility.initialX = 200m
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[1].mobility.initialY = 620m
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[1].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 2
# Association is by best signal and then frozen.
**.dynamicCellAssociation = true
**.enableHandover = false
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 800m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1500m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one NLOS path loss and nothing else ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = false
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false

############### The budget terms, stated rather than inherited, and apart ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
*.gnb1.**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
*.gnb2.**.eNodeBTxPower = 37dBm
**.ueTxPower = 25dBm
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
*.gnb1.cellularNic.radio.antenna.gain = 17dBi
*.gnb2.cellularNic.radio.antenna.gain = 15dBi
*.gnb*.cellularNic.radio.receiver.noiseFigure = 4dB
*.gnb*.cellularNic.radio.receiver.cableLoss = 1dB
*.ue[*].cellularNic.*adio.antenna.gain = 1dBi
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].radio.antenna.gain = 3dBi
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].radio.noiseFigure = 9dB
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].radio.cableLoss = 3.5dB
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[0].generator.txPower = 21dBm

############### Traffic: the first cell's background UEs and the second cell's real UE, both directions ##############
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.typename = "TrafficGeneratorCbr"
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.rtxRateDl = 0
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.rtxRateUl = 0
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.startTimeDl = 0.1s
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.packetSizeDl = 1000B
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.periodDl = 0.011s
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.startTimeUl = 0.1s
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.packetSizeUl = 1000B
*.gnb1.cellularNic.bgTrafficGenerator[0].bgUE[*].generator.periodUl = 0.013s

*.ue[0].numApps = 2
*.server.numApps = 2
*.ue[0].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[0].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 1000B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.007s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.ue[0].app[1].typename = "CbrSender"
*.ue[0].app[1].destAddress = "server"
*.ue[0].app[1].destPort = 4000
*.ue[0].app[1].localPort = 4088
*.ue[0].app[1].packetSize = 1000B
*.ue[0].app[1].samplingTime = 0.007s
*.ue[0].app[1].startTime = 0.1s
*.server.app[1].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.server.app[1].localPort = 4000

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=21 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
